{"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/ChoosingASearchTree","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/TriesAndSuffixStructures","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/DecisionDiagrams","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/RangeAndSpatialTrees"],"title":"Guides","generated":true,"anchor":"Guides"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The collections keep their vertices in flat arrays private to each type. To look at a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"collection’s shape, convert it to the Grafluent type of that shape. The conversion is an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"initializer on the Grafluent type and costs O(","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"text":") once; the result is a snapshot, and later","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edits to the collection don’t reach it:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import GrafluentCollections","import Trees","","var primes: AVLTree = [2, 3, 5]","let shape = BinaryTree(primes)!   \/\/ nil when the collection is empty","primes.insert(7)","shape.vertexCount                 \/\/ 3"]},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Collection"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Grafluent type","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AVLTree"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AVLDictionary"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RedBlackTree"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Treap"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SplayTree"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinaryTree"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistentTreeSet"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistentTreeDictionary"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinaryTree"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BTree"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BTreeDictionary"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RootedTree"},{"type":"text","text":", one vertex per node"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrieDictionary"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrefixTree"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RadixTree"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RadixTreeDictionary"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"SuffixTree","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RootedTree"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SuffixAutomaton"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence"},{"type":"text","text":" (the suffix-link tree)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FenwickTree"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Arborescence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (the update tree)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"SegmentTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"LazySegmentTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"IntervalTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"KDTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Rope","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"BinaryTree","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Quadtree","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Octree","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"MXCIFQuadtree","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"MXCIFOctree","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RootedTree"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LRUCache"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RootedTree"},{"type":"text","text":" (the recency order, a path)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A structure whose shape is not a tree offers a view instead: a Grafluent graph over the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"collection’s own storage, made in O(1). ","type":"text"},{"code":"BinaryDecisionDiagram.graphView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram.graphView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are the diagrams’ tables, ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkipList.layersView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"skip list’s levels, ","type":"text"},{"code":"AhoCorasickAutomaton.statesView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the automaton with its failure links,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and ","type":"text"},{"code":"SuffixAutomaton.transitionsView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"SuffixTree.suffixLinksView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are those structures’","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other edges.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Writing-the-shape","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Writing the shape"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Grafluent’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GraphFormats"},{"type":"text","text":" module writes any graph as DOT, GraphML, GEXF, node-link JSON, an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge list, an adjacency list or Mermaid. An "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps every edge pointing from parent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to child:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import GraphFormats","","let primes: AVLTree = [2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17]","let shape = Arborescence(BinaryTree(primes)!)","var text = \"\"","try shape.writeMermaid(to: &text)","print(text)"]},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["flowchart TD","    7","    3","    13","    2","    5","    11","    17","    7 --> 3","    7 --> 13","    3 --> 2","    3 --> 5","    13 --> 11","    13 --> 17"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"writeDOT(to:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gives Graphviz input the same way, with closures for each vertex’s ID and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attributes when the default descriptions won’t do.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Drawing-the-shape","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Drawing the shape"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Grafluent’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GraphDrawing"},{"type":"text","text":" module lays out a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RootedTree"},{"type":"text","text":" with Reingold and Tilford’s tidy"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"drawing: the root at the origin, each depth one unit lower, and every parent centred over its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"children."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import GraphDrawing","","let tree = RootedTree(Arborescence(BinaryTree(primes)!))","let drawing = tree.reingoldTilfordLayout()","drawing.position(of: 7)     \/\/ (0, 0)","drawing.position(of: 3)     \/\/ (-1, 1)","drawing.position(of: 17)    \/\/ (1.5, 2)"]},{"anchor":"Running-an-algorithm","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Running an algorithm"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A converted shape or a view is an ordinary Grafluent graph, so its traversals, shortest paths and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tree algorithms take it as they would any other:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var diagram = BinaryDecisionDiagram(variableCount: 2)","_ = diagram.and(diagram.variable(0), diagram.variable(1))","let view = diagram.graphView      \/\/ a DirectedGraph over the diagram's table","view.vertexCount                  \/\/ 5: two terminals and three decisions","view.edgeCount                    \/\/ 6"]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/seeingacollectionasagraph"]}],"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Convert a collection’s shape to a Grafluent graph, then lay it out, write it or run an algorithm","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"over it.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections"]]},"metadata":{"title":"Seeing a collection as a graph","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"GrafluentCollections"}]},"references":{"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections/TriesAndSuffixStructures":{"role":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Search a set of keys by prefix, or a text by substring."}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/triesandsuffixstructures","identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/TriesAndSuffixStructures","title":"Tries and suffix structures"},"doc://GrafluentCollections/doc